adjudication.rationale:
Real issue. The new helper `parseRefreshTokenResponse` (packages/app-store/_utils/oauth/parseRefreshTokenResponse.ts) returns the full Zod `safeParse` result object (`{ success, data, error? }`), not the parsed `data`. In GoogleCalendarService the code now does:

```ts
const key = parseRefreshTokenResponse(googleCredentials, googleCredentialSchema);
await prisma.credential.update({ data: { key } });
```

So `credential.key` will be stored as the safeParse wrapper instead of the credential payload shape expected by `googleCredentialSchema`. That will break subsequent uses that assume `credential.key` matches the schema (e.g., future `googleCredentialSchema.parse(...)` or casts), because the top-level object will have `success/data` keys rather than `access_token/refresh_token/...`.
